  "term": "cannabinoid",
  "definition": "A cannabinoid is any compound that can activate the body’s CB1 and/or CB2 cannabinoid receptors. This group includes plant-derived, naturally occurring in-body, and synthetic or partly synthetic compounds, and some can produce psychoactive effects such as euphoria.",
